WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.256
Who adds the next block is decided by consensus.

2
00:00:03.256 --> 00:00:08.341
In proof of work, the right goes to whoever first finds the required number by brute

3
00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:11.187
force, and that costs hardware and electricity.

4
00:00:11.187 --> 00:00:15.545
In proof of stake, blocks are proposed by validators who put up a stake,

5
00:00:15.545 --> 00:00:17.846
and for cheating they lose part of it.

6
00:00:18.846 --> 00:00:20.916
Both methods share one weak spot:

7
00:00:20.916 --> 00:00:22.170
the majority attack.

8
00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:26.875
Whoever controls more than half of the power, or a large part of the stake,

9
00:00:26.875 --> 00:00:30.450
can rewrite recent blocks and spend the same coins twice.

10
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:35.343
In big networks this costs billions; in small ones such attacks have happened.

11
00:00:35.343 --> 00:00:40.110
That is why an exchange credits a transfer only after several confirmations.
